{
  "recap": "Neural networks can be analyzed using a spectral perspective by decomposing their weight matrices into Singular Value Decomposition (SVD). The spectral norm measures how much a matrix can scale a unit input vector, which is a way of quantifying the matrix's size. This concept is generalized to the RMS-to-RMS operator norm, which is a natural choice for deep learning because it helps keep activation vectors well-behaved.",
