{
  "recap": "To model arbitrarily long sequences, researchers compare architectures like recurrence, convolution, and attention. Standard self-attention, however, has a quadratic computational complexity ($O(N^2)$) that becomes prohibitive for very long inputs. To overcome this, various methods have been developed, including sparsification, local/global attention, and integrating external knowledge bases.",
