    {
      "key_point": "S12.K2",
      "question": "How do advanced transformer methods like Reformer and Performer manage to reduce the computational load of attention?",
      "answer": "They achieve this by decomposing the attention mechanism, often using low-rank matrix approximations. This allows them to avoid calculating every possible pairwise interaction, reducing complexity."
