  ]
}

{
  "recap": "Autoregressive models predict the next element in a sequence, such as a word or a pixel, based on all the data that came before it. The probability of the entire sequence is calculated by multiplying the conditional probabilities of each element given its predecessors. This mechanism can be applied to various domains, including language and image processing, and is trained by maximizing the likelihood of the training data.",
