{
  "recap": "Graph Neural Networks (Graph Nets) update a node's vector representation through a series of layers. Each layer involves two steps: neighbors pass messages to each other, and these messages are aggregated to modify the node's current vector. The aggregation function must be permutation-invariant, ensuring that the resulting message is the same regardless of the order in which the neighbors are processed.",
