    },
    {
      "key_point": "S6.K2",
      "question": "How do autoregressive models mathematically represent the probability of an entire sequence of tokens?",
      "answer": "They decompose the joint probability using the chain rule, calculating the probability of each token given all the preceding tokens."
    },
    {
      "key_point": "S6.K3",
      "question": "If a diffusion model uses greedy denoising step-by-step, why might the final output not be the most likely estimate of the original image?",
      "answer": "Since each step maximizes only the conditional probability of slightly less noisy data, this local optimization does not guarantee the highest probability at the end of the entire sequence."
